B. a SkypeSettings.xml file.
on applying a custom theme to Teams Rooms on Windows:

1. Create the SkypeSettings.xml file:

Open a text editor and create a new file named "SkypeSettings.xml".
Paste the following XML structure, adjusting the image path and color values:
XML
&lt;SkypeSettings&gt;
    &lt;Theming&gt;
        &lt;ThemeName&gt;Custom&lt;/ThemeName&gt;
        &lt;CustomThemeImageUrl&gt;C:\Users\Skype\AppData\Local\Packages\Microsoft.SkypeRoomSystem_8wekyb3d8bbwe\LocalState\YourCustomImage.jpg&lt;/CustomThemeImageUrl&gt;
        &lt;CustomThemeColor&gt;
            &lt;RedComponent&gt;255&lt;/RedComponent&gt;
            &lt;GreenComponent&gt;255&lt;/GreenComponent&gt;
            &lt;BlueComponent&gt;255&lt;/BlueComponent&gt;
        &lt;/CustomThemeColor&gt;
    &lt;/Theming&gt;
&lt;/SkypeSettings&gt;

Set-CsPhoneNumberAssignment is the only option that allows you to define the phone number type. The supported values are DirectRouting, CallingPlan, and OperatorConnect

Set-CsPhoneNumberAssignment
   -Identity &lt;string&gt;
   -PhoneNumber &lt;string&gt;
   -PhoneNumberType &lt;String&gt;
   -Notify
   [&lt;CommonParameters&gt;]

Source link: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/powershell/module/teams/set-csphonenumberassignment?view=teams-ps

To disable room auto-accept for QR code meeting joins on your Teams Rooms on Windows, you can add the following to your XML configuration profile:
To disable room auto-accept for QR code meeting joins on your Teams Rooms on Windows, you can add the following to your XML configuration profile:

&lt;QRCodeAutoAcceptProximateMeetingInvitations&gt;false&lt;/QRCodeAutoAcceptProximateMeetingInvitations&gt;
